$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3',4'-Dihexyl-2,2'-bithiophene-4-carbaldehyde (S2): To a solution of
5-bromo-3-thiophenecarbaldehyde (3.100 g, 16.2 mmol), K2CO3 (4.494 g,
32.5 mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (914 mg, 0.791 mmol) in toluene/water (3/1, 20
mL) was added a solution of boronic acid ester S1 (6.623 g 18.2 mmol) in
THF (15 mL). The reaction mixture was heated to reflux and stirred for 2
days. After cooling to room temperature, water (20 mL) was added to the
reaction mixture. The aqueous layer was extracted with diethyl ether (3 ×
30 mL). The combined organic extracts were washed with water (1 × 10 mL)
and brine (1 × 10 mL), then dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. After filtration
and removal of solvent in vacuo, the crude product was purified by column
chromatography (silica gel, EtOAc/n-hexane = 1/25) to give product.
Yield:97% (5.678 g), pale yellow oil. 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.88 (s,
1H), 8.05 (d, J = 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.49 (d.J = 1.4 Hz, 1H), 6.91 (s, 1H),
2.67 (t, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 2.53 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 2H), 1.65 (quin, J = 7.7
Hz, 2H), 1.53-1.47 (m, 2H), 1.44-1.22 (m, 12H), 0.92-0.86 (m, 6H);
13C-NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 184.83, 143.64, 143.03, 140.15, 139.29,
136.04, 129.26, 123.12, 120.16, 31.71, 31.47, 30.40, 29.68, 29.42, 29.26,
29.18, 27.59, 22.60, 22.56, 14.05, 14.01; HRMS (ESI-Orbitrap): m/z calcd
for C21H30OS2Na, 385.1630; found, 385.1635 ([M+Na]+).
