$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 2. A biphasic suspension of potassium
N-Boc-indole-2-trifluoroborate (1) (621 mg, 1.92 mmol),
3-amino-6-bromopyridine (480 mg, 1.74 mmol), and Na2CO3 (462 mg, 4.35
mmol) in 1,2-dimethoxyethane (20 mL) and water (5 mL) was purged with
nitrogen for 15 min. Tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (200 mg,
0.17 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture heated to 86 °C overnight.
The resulting yellow suspension was cooled to ambient temperature,
diluted with water and extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic layers
were washed with brine, dried using Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated to
dryness in vacuo. The crude material was purified by silica gel
chromatography using DCM/MeOH (15:1). Compound 2 was obtained as a yellow
solid, yield 533 mg, 1.71 mmol, 97%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm)
8.14-8.16 (m, 2H), 7.54 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.23-7.32 (m, 3H), 7.00 (dd,
J = 8.4, 3.0 Hz, 1H), 6.67 (s, 1H), 3.75 (br s, 2H) 1.39 (s, 9H). 13C NMR
(75 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) 150.2, 142.7, 142.3, 139.2, 137.3, 135.7, 129.0,
124.5, 124.0, 122.8, 121.6, 120.7, 114.9, 110.0, 83.4, 27.6. IR (film): ν
(cm-1) 3374, 3208, 2980, 1727, 1625, 1593, 1485, 1451, 1366, 1327, 1229,
1159, 1134, 1031, 1016, 849, 816, 693. HRMS: calcd for C18H20N3O2 (M +
H)+ 310.1550, found (M + H)+ 310.1549.
