$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7-tert-Butoxycarbonyl-2-exo-[2′ -amino-3′ -(pyridin-4-yl)-5′
-pyridinyl]-7-azabicyclo[2.2.1]heptane (12a). A solution of compound 9
(354 mg, 0 0.96 mmol, 1.0 equiv), pyridine-4-boronic acid (154 mg, 1.25
mmol, 1.3 equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (56 mg, 0.048 mmol, 5 mol %), and K2CO3 (266
mg, 1.92 mmol, 2.0 equiv) in toluene (10 mL), EtOH (2 mL), and water (2
mL) was degassed through bubbling nitrogen for 20 min. The mixture was
sealed and heated over a sand bath at 110 °C for 22 h. After cooling to
room temperature, 20 mL of H2O was added, and the organic product was
extracted with EtOAc (3 × 30 mL). The combined organic layers were dried
over MgSO4, filtered through Celite, and concentrated in vacuo. The
resultant residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel
using i-PrOH-hexanes as the eluent to provide 12a. yield 340 mg, 97%. 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.39 (br s, 9H), 1.44-1.59 (m, 2H), 1.81-1.84 (m,
3H), 1.93-2.00 (m, 1H), 2.79-2.84 (dd, J= 3.8, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 4.16 (s, 1H),
4.36 (br s, 1H), 4.67 (s, 2 NH), 7.39-7.43 (m, 3H), 7.99 (d, J= 2.3 Hz,
1H), 8.66 (dd, J= 6.0, 1.5 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 28.3 (3 C), 28.8,
29.7, 40.4, 44.8, 55.8, 62.1, 79.5, 118.7, 123.4 (2 C), 132.2, 136.5,
146.4, 147.2, 150.5 (2 C), 153.9, 154.9; MS (ESI) m/z 367.6 (M + H)+.
