$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-Chloro-N-[1-methyl-4-(3-thienyl)-1H-indazol-3-yl]-2-thiophenesulfonamide
(58) 1-Methyl-4-(3-thienyl)-1H-indazol-3-amine: A solution of
4-bromo-1-methyl-1H-indazol-3-amine (226 mg, 1.00 mmol) in 1,4-dioxane
(10 mL) was added to a microwave vessel containing 3-thienylboronic acid
(192 mg, 1.50 mmol) and 2'-(dimethylamino)-2-biphenyl-palladium(II)
chloride dinorbornylphosphine complex (2.80 mg, 5.00 Xmol). A solution of
tri-potassium phosphate (212 mg, 1.00 mmol) in water (2 mL) was added and
the vessel was sealed and heated in Biotage Initiator using initial high
to 120 °C for 30 minutes. After cooling the reaction mixture was dried
under a stream of nitrogen in the Radleys blow-down apparatus to give the
crude product. The sample was purified by chromatography on silica (20 g)
eluting with a gradient of 0-100% ethyl acetatecyclohexane over 30
minutes. The appropriate fractions were combined and evaporated in vacuo
to give the title compound. (220 mg, 96%) as a yellow solid. LCMS (System
A)RT = 0.94 min, ES+ve m/z 230 (M+ H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki-type coupling, sealed vessel used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Structure-Activity Relationships of Indazole
Arylsulfonamides as Allosteric CC-Chemokine Receptor 4 (CCR4) Antagonists
