$DATUM Compound 8. A mixture of compound 7 (1.70 g, 4.24 mmol),
bis(pinacolato)diboron (1.291 g, 5.08 mmol), Pd(dppf)Cl2 (346 mg, 0.423
mmol) and KOAc (1.247 g, 12.71 mmol) in degassed 1,4-dioxane (30 mL) was
stirred at 100°C for 24 h under argon. The reaction mixture was cooled to
r.t., filtered to remove the inorganic compound. The filtrate was
evaporated to dryness and the residue was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc = 2:1). The product was obtained as a light
yellow oil (1.826 g, 96%). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ (ppm) 7.78 (d, J1 = 2.5 Hz,
1H), 7.53 (d, J2 = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 7.48 (d, J1 = 2.5 Hz, 1H), 6.91 (d, J2 =
7.5 Hz, 2H), 4.15 (t, J3 = 5.0 Hz, 2H), 3.86 (t, J3 = 5.0 Hz, 2H),
3.77-3.63 (m, 6H), 3.58-3.53 (m, 2H), 3.38 (s, 3H), 1.34 (s, 12H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3): δ (ppm) 158.34, 144.64, 135.13, 127.29, 127.16, 126.97,
114.95, 83.73, 71.94, 70.86, 70.68, 70.59, 69.74, 67.51, 59.06, 24.85.
FD-MS (8 KV): m/z 447.70, cacld.: 448.38.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 41% overall yield in 3 steps starting from 2,4-dibromothiophene
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Assembly and Fiber Formation of a Gemini-Type Hexathienocoronene
Amphiphile for Electrical Conduction
