$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 15 Argon gas was bubbled through a heterogeneous mixture of
2,4-dimorpholino-6-chloropyrimidine (1.98 g, 6.90 mmol) and
4-(trifluoromethyl)-5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyridin-2-amine
(8.0 g, 27.8 mmol) in 1,2-dimethoxyethane (45mL) and 2M Na2CO3 (15mL) for
20 minutes. 1,1'-Bis(diphenylphosphino)ferrocene palladium (II) chloride
(170 mg, 0.21 mmol) was added and the high pressure vessel containing the
mixture was sealed. The reaction mixture was then heated at 90 ºC for 15
hours, cooled and diluted with EtOAc (500 mL). The organic solution was
washed with 200 mL of a mixture of Na2CO3 (sat.):Water:NH4OH(conc.) =
5:4:1, then NH4Cl(sat.), and brine (2x), dried over Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated. The crude material was purified by SiO2 chromatography
(50-90% EtOAc/hexanes). 2.70 g (96%) of
5-(2,6-dimorpholinopyrimidin-4-yl)-4-(trifluoromethyl)pyridin-2-amine as
an off-white solid. LCMS (m/z): 411.0 (MH+). HRMS: [M+H]+ calculated
411.1756, found 411.1761. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 8.27 (s, 1H), 6.78 (s, 1H),
5.97 (s, 1H), 4.77 (bs, 2H), 3.59-3.80(m, 12H), 3.58-3.61(m, 4H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki reaction, sealed pressure vessel used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Identification of NVP-BKM120 as a Potent, Selective, Orally Bioavailable
Class I PI3 Kinase Inhibitor for Treating Cancer
