$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Suzuki-Miyaura Cross
Coupling. After a mixture of compound 7 (61 mg, 0.1 mmol), K2CO3 (138 mg,
1 mmol), boronic acid (0.3 mmol) in toluene (18 mL), ethanol (12 mL) and
water (6 mL) was degassed three times and kept under argon atmosphere,
catalytic amount (∼10%) of Pd(PPh3)4 was then added. The resulting
mixture was heated to reflux for 8 h, cooled to room temperature, and
then poured into 5% aqueous hydrochloric acid (15 mL). The mixture was
extracted with dichloromethane (3 × 5 mL), and the combined organic layer
was washed with water and dried over anhydrous MgSO4. The solvent was
removed in vacuo to give a residue, which was purified by chromatography.
7-Isopentyl-2,12-dimethoxy-3,11-di(thiophen-3-yl)-5H-diindeno[
2,1-e:1′,2′-g]isoindole-6,8(7H,9H)-dione (8j). Yellow powder. Yield: 95%.
mp 296-297°C; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.18 (s, 2H), 7.82 (s, 2H), 7.75
(dd, J = 3.0, 1.2 Hz, 2H), 7.55 (dd, J = 5.1, 1.2 Hz, 2H), 7.42 (dd, J =
5.0, 3.0 Hz, 2H), 4.31 (s, 4H), 4.05 (s, 6H), 3.73 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H),
1.69-1.60 (m, 3H), 1.00 (d, J = 6.2 Hz, 6H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
168.2, 155.7, 141.6, 141.4, 139.3, 138.1, 137.7, 128.3, 125.8, 125.6,
124.7, 124.0, 123.6, 107.4, 56.1, 37.4, 36.1, 34.7, 26.1, 22.3; HR ESI-MS
m/z calcd for [M + H+]+ C37H32NO4S2, 618.1767, found 618.1766. Crystal
Data of 8j: Identification code: sa2888; Empirical formula: C37H31NO4S2;
Formula weight: 617.75; Temperature: 173(2) K; Wavelength: 0.71073 Å;
Crystal system, space group: Monoclinic, P2(1)/n; Unit cell dimensions: a
= 17.041(5) Å alpha = 90 deg. b = 9.345(3) Å beta = 100.886(4) deg. c =
19.211(6) Å gamma = 90 deg. Volume 3004.2(15) Å3; Z, Calculated density:
4, 1.361 Mg/m3; Absorption coefficient: 0.221 mm-1; F(000): 1296; Crystal
size: 0.25 x 0.10 x 0.06 mm; Theta range for data collection: 3.07 to
25.00 deg; Limiting indices -20<=h<=17, -11<=k<=11, -22<=l<=22;
Reflections collected / unique: 18100 / 5260 [R(int) = 0.0679];
Completeness to theta = 25.00: 99.7 %; Absorption correction:
Semi-empirical from equivalents; Max. and min. transmission: 1.0000 and
0.6046; Refinement method: Full-matrix least-squares on F2; Data /
restraints / parameters: 5260 / 42 / 420; Goodness-of-fit on F2: 1.101;
Final R indices [I>2sigma(I)]: R1 = 0.0793, wR2 = 0.1621; R indices (all
data): R1 = 0.1004, wR2 = 0.1741; Largest diff. peak and hole: 0.255 and
-0.327 e.Å-3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Dihydroindeno[2,1-c]fluorene-Based Imide Dyes: Synthesis, Structures,
Photophysical and Electrochemical Properties
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Li, Yang-Yang; Lu, Hai-Yan; Li, Meng; Li, Xiao-Jun; Chen, Chuan-Feng
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(5), 2139-2147

