$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Suzuki Cross-Coupling. A
suspension of the pyridyl bromides (1 equiv), Pd(PPh)4 (0.2 equiv), and
boronic acid or boronate ester (1.5 equiv) in dimethoxyethane was
degassed and then flashed with Argon. A solution of 2 M K2CO3 (2.5 equiv)
was added, and the mixture was flushed again with Argon. The reaction
mixture was stirred at 80°C for 15 h. The solution was filtered through
Celite, and the Celite was rinsed with 5% MeOH in EtOAc (3×). The eluents
were concentrated and the residue was purified by silica gel
chromatography using a CombiFlash instrument and a solvent gradient from
1:1 EtOAc/hexanes to 100% EtOAc and then to 20% MeOH in EtOAc.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, Suzuki coupling, may use boronate ester in place of
boronic acid
