$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
7-(2,3-O-Isopropylidene-5-O-tert-butyldimethylsilyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-4-phenyl-7H-pyrrolo[
2,3-d]pyrimidine (10d). An argon purged mixture of compound 8 (309 mg,
0.7 mmol), phenylboronic acid (128 mg, 1.05 mmol), K2CO3 (193 mg, 1.4
mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (41 mg, 0.035 mmol) in toluene (5 mL) was stirred at
100 °C for 5 h. The mixture was diluted with chloroform (20 mL) and
washed with aqueous NH4Cl (sat., 20 mL). The aqueous phase was
re-extracted with chloroform (2×5 mL) and the combined organic extracts
dried over MgSO4, concentrated in vacuo and the residue chromatographed
on silica (hexanes-AcOEt, 10:1→7:1) to afford 10d (320 mg, 95%) as a
colorless oil.
7-(2,3-O-Isopropylidene-5-O-tert-butyldimethylsilyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-4-(pyridin-3-yl)-
7H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine (10g). Compound 10g was prepared as described
for 10d by coupling compound 8 (0.695 mmol) and pyridine-3-boronic acid,
but dimethoxyethane/H2O (3:1, 4 mL) was used as solvent instead of
toluene. Column chromatography on silica gel eluting with hexanes-AcOEt,
2:1 provided 10g as a yellowish oil. Yield 95%. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3):
0.07 and 0.08 (2 × s, 2 × 3H, CH3Si); 0.91 (s, 9H, (CH3)3C); 1.41 and
1.67 (2 × q, 2 × 3H, J = 0.6, (CH3)2C); 3.82 (dd, 1H, J gem= 11.3, J
5´b,4´= 3.7, H-5´b); 3.92 (dd, 1H, J gem= 11.3,J 5´a,4´ = 3.6, H-5´a);
4.38 (ddd, 1H, J 4´,5´ = 3.7, 3.6,J 4´,3´ = 3.1, H-4´); 4.99 (ddd, 1H, J
3´,2´ = 6.2, J 3´,4´ = 3.1, J 3´,1´ = 0.4, H-3´); 5.13 (dd, 1H, J 2´,3´ =
6.2, J 2´,1´ = 3.0, H-2´); 6.51 (d, 1H, J 1´,2´ = 3.0, H-1´); 6.84 (d,
1H, J 5,6 = 3.8, H-5); 7.50 (ddd, 1H,J 5,4 = 7.9, J 5,6 = 4.6, J 5,2 J
5,2 = 0.9, H-5-py); 7.65 (d, 1H, J 6,5 = 3.8, H-6); 8.43 (ddd, 1H, J 4,5
= 7.9, J 4,2= 2.2, J4,6 = 1.7, H- 4-py); 8.75 (dd, 1H, J 6,5 = 4.6, J 6,4
= 1.7, H-6-py); 9.01 (s, 1H, H-2); 9.33 (dd, 1H,J 2,4 = 2.2, J 2,5= 0.9,
H-2-py). 13C NMR (151 MHz, CDCl3): -5.49 and -5.38 (CH3Si); 18.38
(C(CH3)3); 25.47 ((CH3)2C); 25.90 ((CH3)3C); 27.37 ((CH3)2C); 63.42
(CH2-5´); 80.89 (CH-3´); 85.06 (CH-2´); 86.10 (CH-4´); 90.30 (CH-1´);
100.83 (CH-5); 114.20 (C(CH3)2); 116.54 (C-4a); 123.79 (CH-5-py); 127.48
(CH-6); 133.92 (C-3-py); 136.08 (CH-4-py); 149.81 (CH-2-py); 150.84
(CH-6-py); 151.65 (C-7a); 151.79 (CH-2); 154.63 (C-4). MS FAB, m/z (rel.
%): 73 (45), 196 (35), 483 (100)[M+H]; HR MS (FAB): calcd for
C25H35N4O4Si [M+H] 483.2428, found 483.2433.
