$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 12) Procedure for the preparation of
9-(thiophen-3-yl)-2,3-dihydro-1H-cyclopenta[b]quinoline (4e) A sealed
tube was charged with the mixture of 9-bromo-2,3-dihydro-1Hcyclopenta[
b]quinoline (1.0 mmol, 247 mg), 3-thiopheneboronic acid (1.2 mmol, 153.6
mg), Pd(PPh3)4 (3 mol%, 34.7 mg) and K2CO3 (2.0 mmol, 276.4 mg). The tube
was evacuated and recharged with N2 for 3 times. After THF:H2O (1:1, 5.0
mL) was added, the tube was sealed and the mixture was allowed to stir at
85 °C for 12 h. After completion, the mixture was cooled to room
temperature, then K2CO3 aq. (5 mL) was added and the mixture was
extracted with DCM (5 mL x 3), dried by anhydrous Na2SO4. Evaporation of
the solvent followed by purification on silica gel (petroleum
ether/diethyl ether/triethylamine: 40/2/1) provided the corresponding
product as a yellow solid.19
9-(thiophen-3-yl)-2,3-dihydro-1H-cyclopenta[b]quinoline (4e): yellow
solid, 239 mg, yield: 95%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CHLOROFORM-D) δ 7.95 (d, J =
8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.67 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.49 (dd, J = 8.1, 7.1 Hz, 1H),
7.35 (dd, J = 4.8, 2.9 Hz, 1H), 7.31 - 7.21 (m, 2H), 7.11 - 7.04 (m, 1H),
3.09 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 2.82 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 2.02 (p, J = 7.5 Hz,
2H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CHLOROFORM-D) δ 167.48, 148.07, 137.85, 136.74,
134.08, 128.99, 128.98, 128.33, 126.39, 125.83, 125.63, 125.57, 124.86,
35.31, 30.79, 23.61. ESI-HRMS: m/z calcd for C16H13NS[M+H]+: 252.0841;
found: 252.0840.
