$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6'-Methoxy-3-trifluoromethyl[2,3']bipyridinyl (19). A mixture of
2-chloro-3-trifluoromethylpyridine (8) (37 g, 0.2 mol),
2-methoxypyridine-5-boronic acid (32 g, 0.21 mol),
tetrakis-(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (9 g, 7 mmol), and 2 M
potassium carbonate (150 mL) in toluene (500 mL) was heated, under a
nitrogen atmosphere, at 90°C for 8 h. The reaction mixture was cooled,
and the layers were separated. The aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl
acetate (2 x 250 mL), and the combined extracts were washed with 4 M
sodium hydroxide (250 mL), water (250 mL), brine (250 mL), dried (MgSO4),
and concentrated under reduced pressure. The oil was purified by flash
chromatography (elution with ether/hexane, 1:1) and gave the title
compound 19 (48.2 g, 95%), a colorless oil.
6'-Methoxy-3-trifluoromethyl[2,3']bipyridinyl, yield (48.2 g, 95%). MS
255 (M + 1). 1H NMR δ (CDCl3) 8.85 (1H, d, J = 5 Hz), 8.34 (1H, s), 8.09
(1H, d, J = 7.5 Hz), 7.76 (1H, dd, J = 2.5 and 8.5 Hz), 7.46-7.41 (1H,
m), 6.82 (1H, d, J = 8 Hz), 3.76 (3H, s).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Novel 6,6-Heterocycles as Transient Receptor Potential
Vanilloid (TRPV1) Antagonists
